+### Remodel mode (verbatim IA)
+
+When the resolved direction pins the information architecture
+verbatim — `DESIGN.json.extensions.iaPriorities[]` is present and
+every entry has `mutability: "locked"` (the stamp `direct` writes
+for "same IA, swap the surface" directions) — the stock compose
+path is wrong for the run: the current page's rendered HTML is the
+canonical document, and the redesign must preserve its structure,
+IDs, accessibility hooks, analytics attributes, and integrations.
+Prototype switches to **remodel mode** for every page in scope.
+
+**Detection (Setup step 7).** After Setup step 6, read
+`DESIGN.json.extensions.iaPriorities`. If present and every entry
+has `mutability: "locked"`, set remodel mode and surface
+`Remodel mode: verbatim IA pinned by direction`. Otherwise
+continue stock. Remodel mode requires a remodeled impeccable
+(the impeccable skill ships `reference/remodel.md`, e.g. the
+impeccable-remodel fork build); if absent, stop and recommend
+installing it — stock craft regenerates from scratch and would
+destroy the hooks this mode exists to preserve. Do not fall back
+to the compose path silently.
+
+**Flow (replaces Phases 1–2 for the run):**
+
+1. Skip the page-shape brief and `$impeccable shape` — structure
+   is fixed by the source document.
+2. Lazy-capture the canonical markup: playwright `page.content()`
+   of the page record's `url` from `stardust/state.json`, written
+   to `stardust/current/pages/<slug>.html`. Reuse an existing
+   capture from the same calendar day.
+3. Copy the capture to
+   `stardust/prototypes/<slug>-proposed.html`. The capture stays
+   pristine as the before for the invariant gate.
+4. Invoke `$impeccable craft stardust/prototypes/<slug>-proposed.html`
+   with the resolved direction (DESIGN.md / DESIGN.json, plus
+   direction.md § Anti-references and § Divergence inputs as hard
+   constraints) as the brief. Craft's remodel detection fires on
+   the HTML file target and edits in place.
+5. Run the invariant gate when available:
+   `node <impeccable-remodel-clone>/scripts/remodel-check.mjs stardust/current/pages/<slug>.html stardust/prototypes/<slug>-proposed.html`
+   must report 0 immutable violations (ids, `data-*`, `aria-*`,
+   form names, scripts, template markers). The script ships with
+   the remodeled impeccable (its fork clone's `scripts/`); if not
+   found, print a warning and continue — craft's own per-pass
+   invariant self-check still applies.
+6. Quality gates (Phases 2.5–2.8), Phase 4, and Phase 5 run
+   unchanged. State bookkeeping is stock.
+
+**Contract deltas from `reference/proposed-file-shell.md`**
+(remodel mode only):
+
+- Self-containment: relaxed. The source document's existing
+  external references (CSS, JS, fonts, CMS assets) are preserved,
+  not inlined. New CSS craft adds lives in an embedded `<style>`
+  or in edits to existing referenced stylesheets.
+- Provenance block: emitted as an HTML comment at the top of
+  `<head>`, not a DOM element (zero-churn provenance).
+- Structural data attributes: additive-only — never rename, strip,
+  or reorder existing attributes; required stardust data
+  attributes are added where absent.
+- `:root` token block: still required; craft adds it in the
+  embedded style surface.
+- Content sourcing: the source HTML is the strongest provenance
+  tier — every literal must trace to the source document or a
+  direction-authorised change; anything else carries the
+  placeholder signature. The scan runs against the capture, not
+  `pages/<slug>.json`.
+- Structure: DOM hierarchy, IDs, existing `data-*` / `aria-*`,
+  form names, event hooks, and scripts are immutable (enforced by
+  craft's remodel invariants plus the gate in step 5).
+
